    49	## 3. How it's built
    50	
    51	| # | Choice | Recommendation | Why |
    52	|---|---|---|---|
    53	| B1 | Technology | Plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript modules; no framework, no app build. A deploy step copies shared files in (§4). Node + Playwright only for checks and tests | Production is React Native, so prototype code isn't reused — easy to read and change |
    54	| B2 | Location | New folder `app/` in the project; old files untouched | Clean start; old demo keeps working |
    55	| B3 | Structure | One file per screen, one per sheet, plus a small core: navigation, app state, copy (`MSG()`), mock server, call simulator, clock, settings, mock phone unlock | Each journey built, checked and frozen on its own |
    56	| B4 | States and addressing **[R]** | One **state map**: journey, state ID, scenario, render ID, picture (or "behaviour only"), build step, transitions to test. Every state, incl. behaviour-only ones (`offer.cancelled`, `offer.not-now`, `offer.unsupported`, `offer.enabled`, `rx.load-failed`, `case.reopened`, hold / mismatch), opens with `?s=<id>`. Calling rows generated from `calling-flow/data.js` with a **normalising step**: one owner per picture, Pilot retries keep Pilot context (`data.js` draws 6 → Call again and 7b → Still talking into the Cat4 lane), joins resolved, backend-only outcomes kept. A drift check fails if the map and `data.js` disagree; the map is also checked once against app-logic §5 before step 1 (a match with `data.js` doesn't prove `data.js` right). Retired keys (`call.forwarded-after-hangup`, `call.end-call-first`, `case.end-call-first`) not carried. Header shows the source versions (calling-flow page, D-85) | One source for the calling flow; drift visible |
    57	| B5 | Look | Only `truemeds.css`, `icons.js`, `--tm-*` tokens, `.tm-*` components; markup lifted from the approved `ui-screens/` files; icons from the design system, never emoji | Screens come out the same as the pictures |
    58	| B6 | Copy | Every word through `MSG()` from `messages.json` (copy annex applied, D-84). Labels still typed in the pictures move into the registry in the step that builds them. Copy-rule checks run on `app/` | One source of copy for HTML and native |
    59	| B7 | Server and polling **[R]** | Mock server plays the backend; the app polls it (`[MOCK ASSUMPTION]`), one loop per case and call; stale or duplicate answers ignored; a late answer for an earlier case never updates the open one; re-reads the case when the app returns to the front. Partner rules (D-83 pt 7): **5 Getting call result only for Pilot after the partner reports the hang-up — Cat4 never reaches 5**; 7b only when the end can't be known, otherwise the 3-min timeout goes straight to 7c. Whether Knowlarity sends a call-ended event is **open** (Engineering) — a simulator switch, default "no event" | Same shape as the real system |
    60	| B8 | Clock and gate | One app clock; the gate worked out from time stamps (patient answered → now), never a counter. Talk time adds up across counted calls (B10) | Phones pause timers in the background |
    61	| B9 | Call simulator **[R]** | Review panel picks per call: connected (above / under the gate, length) · doctor-side failure (3, 4) · patient-side failure by cause (busy / no answer / switched off / network → retried; unknown → plain hold; invalid number → not retried, flagged) → 9 · partner (Ozonetel / Knowlarity) + Knowlarity call-ended event on/off · hang-up reported / not · who ended (doctor / patient / unknown → 16 / 16b / 16c) · B2: HA free / no HA free / transfer request failed (→ 15) · HA doesn't pick up (→ 14 for the doctor) · call record: arrives over the gate / under the gate / patient never answered / never, with a delay · callback refused (leg 2 never answered) · release refused after the call request was accepted | Every D-83 branch reachable without code changes |
    62	| B10 | Settings **[R]** | One settings file. Rules: gate 50 s · no-result timeout 3 min, 7b repeats every 3 min · counted call ≥ ~10 s, talk-time window ~30 min (D-58 pt 22). `[MOCK ASSUMPTION]`: call-record wait 30 min · hold-retry gap 15 min and attempts 3 · polling every 3 s (inside D-58 pt 14's "about 5 s") · OTP window 10 min, lock 15 min, resend waits 30 / 60 / 120 s (OQ-017) · near-expiry warning 5 min · returning unlock falls back to OTP after 3 failures. **Demo scales every time value** by one factor (gate, ~10 s minimum, 30-min window, timeouts, waits, polling), so an 8 s demo call still passes | Nothing hard-coded; real rules vs stand-ins visible |
    63	| B11 | Data | Synthetic only: four launch scenarios + stress (10 medicines, long names, empty case); test numbers and codes from app-logic §11 in one data file the tests read | No real patient, phone or doctor data |
    64	| B12 | Remembering **[R]** | The installed app remembers sign-in, faster sign-in, availability and an open case: medicines reviewed, notes typed, deadlines, call stage. Session stays valid through an open case (no OTP over a live case). Demo and review keep separate storage; capture writes nothing; Reset and Log out clear it | Reopening must feel real (production: OQ-025) |
    65	| B13 | Phone back **[R]** | Every screen and sheet is a step in the app's history. In a case: header Back per §0 "Back on a case"; during a call phone back shows the toast; on a closed case phone back goes Home; never closes the app mid-case | Otherwise back closes the installed app |
    66	| B14 | Phone unlock | Mock: the review panel picks success / cancelled / failed / unavailable; the demo succeeds | A browser can't use the phone's unlock like the native app |
    67	| B15 | Checks | Playwright. Step 0 points `layout_check.py` at `app/` on a local server; adds the screenshot compare (390 + 360, fixed clock, frozen animations, spinner mask) and journey tests, incl. one test per calling-flow edge generated from the state map, and a play-link test for each launch scenario (the same story through the link and through the desktop panel ends in the same state) **[R2]**. Every step runs G7 | The current layout check tests the old `index.html` |
