    69	## 4. Modes, install and hosting [R]
    70	
    71	- **Review mode (bare link):** panel beside the frame (RULES §7.5) — scenario, call simulator (B9), phone-unlock outcome, jump to any state, fast-forward, offline / failure switches, width 360 / 390, reset, event log (four confirm outcomes as separate events, once per completed confirm, D-50; mismatch events).
    72	- **Phone testing [R2]:** on a phone the review panel never sits on top of the app.
    73	  - **Play link (QR):** the desktop review panel has a "Test on phone" section covering **every journey**, not only calling (clarified 2026-11-06, D-89): where the story starts (sign-in, returning unlock, Home, or straight into a case) and what each step answers — sign-in result (sent / not registered / inactive / too many tries / couldn't send / locked), OTP result (correct / wrong / expired / couldn't verify / resend outcomes), faster sign-in and unlock outcomes, offline moments, Home (availability near expiry or ending, request fails, no cases), the case (normal, 10 medicines, long names, empty case, Rx fails, release refused), Prescribe and confirm outcomes, and the call story (call outcome per attempt, partner, who ends the call, HA free or not, call record). It shows a QR code and a short link (`?play=<code>`, the story written into the link; no server). Scanned on the phone, the app opens full screen and plays that story as the tester taps through — outcomes arrive by themselves at realistic times. Opens in the phone's browser (the installed app stays demo-only). An unreadable code opens review with a notice.
    74	  - **Hidden drawer:** in review or play on a narrow screen, a small control handle sits at the screen edge — never over the header controls, the action bar or a sheet. Tapping it slides the controls up from the bottom, **showing the ones for the screen you're on** (sign-in: result; OTP: code result; Home: request outcome; case: call controls), with "Jump to a state" and "Restart story" always there; tapping outside closes it. Not shown in demo or capture.
    75	  - **Later (backlog):** live remote, where the desktop drives the phone in real time — needs a message relay (Netlify function credits or a third-party service).
    76	- **Demo mode (`?demo=1`; the installed app always):** Cat4 happy path, no review controls; the installed app ignores review or capture settings in a link.
    77	- **Capture mode (`?capture=1`):** no panel, screen width only, fixed clock, animations frozen.
    78	- **Folder layout (same locally and deployed):** `app/` holds the app. The deploy step copies in `design-system/` (styles, icons, fonts, logo), the "truemeds for doctors" lockup and the copy registry, so all shared paths resolve inside `app/`; these copies are git-ignored, never committed. Locally: `python3 -m http.server` from the project folder.
    79	- **Install:** manifest (id, scope, name "truemeds for doctors", short name, opens demo, standalone, portrait, theme and background colours); icons 180 / 192 / 512 PNG from `design-system/logo/truemeds-icon.svg` unchanged, mark on white with safe padding; iPhone tags and touch icon; safe areas; no offline cache in the first build; always checks for a new version; hidden from search engines. Android: install from the browser menu; iPhone: Share → Add to Home Screen.
    80	- **Hosting:** second Netlify site **`truemeds-doctor-app-preview`**, from the same repo. Settings: base directory = the project's `app/` folder (its own `netlify.toml` there; the current site's root file untouched); production branch = the project branch, so review needs no merge to `main`; build command = the copy step above; publish = `app/` only (no `docs/`). **Deploy gate:** the same `ignore` rule as the current site — the site builds only when the latest commit message contains `[deploy]`. Claude adds `[deploy]` to a commit only when Apurva asks. Step 0 tests both cases (unmarked commit → skipped, marked → deployed, design-system files load, `docs/` not served). Apurva creates the site — step-by-step guide in step 0.
